These are md2html v0.12.0's own output, kept so TestUnchangedOutput
(highlight_test.go) can check that a page with no highlighted fence is
still what v0.12.0 wrote, once its stylesheet's --syntax-* declarations
are taken out.

Made on 2026-10-15 from tag v0.12.0 (9574390) in a temporary worktree,
with the program below placed at cmd/goldengen/main.go there and run as

    git worktree add --detach /tmp/v0120 v0.12.0
    cd /tmp/v0120 && go run ./cmd/goldengen <this directory>
    git worktree remove --force /tmp/v0120

Each case is converted the way the test's convertBody does: Fragment on
and a Warn function, with no style named, so the default style applies.
v0.12.0 had no NoHighlight option, so "option-off" is converted with
plain options there; today's side turns highlighting off.

Each golden starts with v0.12.0's provenance marker, which names that
version. The test swaps that one marker for today's Marker() before
comparing, so bumping Version does not break it; nothing else in a
golden is rewritten.

The sources must stay the same as the test's. If one changes, or a case
is added, remake the goldens this way rather than editing them by hand.

----- cmd/goldengen/main.go -----
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"os"
	"path/filepath"

	"github.com/AdamF-G/md2html"
)

func main() {
	out := os.Args[1]
	cases := []struct {
		name, src string
		opt       md2html.Options
	}{
		{"no-language", "```\nfunc x\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"unknown-language", "```text\nfunc x\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"no-highlight", "```{.go .no-highlight}\nfunc x\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"front-matter-off", "---\nhighlight: false\n---\n```go\nfunc x\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"option-off", "```go\nfunc x\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"no-code", "# Title\n\nText.\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"fig-falls-back", "```fig\nnot: [a figure\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
		{"vega-lite-off", "```vega-lite\n{\"mark\": \"bar\"}\n```\n", md2html.Options{NoCharts: true}},
		{"mermaid-any-case", "```Mermaid\ngraph LR\n```\n", md2html.Options{}},
	}
	for _, c := range cases {
		c.opt.Fragment = true
		c.opt.Warn = func(s string) { fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "%s: %s\n", c.name, s) }
		b, err := md2html.Convert([]byte(c.src), c.opt)
		if err != nil {
			panic(err)
		}
		if err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(out, c.name+".html"), b, 0o644); err != nil {
			panic(err)
		}
	}
}
